# IOrderBy, OrderBy, and SortDirection

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Persistence`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Persistence.Core`
**Version**: 0.6.0

## Purpose

Ordering types used by `IStore<T>.FindManyAsync` to specify how query results should be sorted.

## `SortDirection`

```csharp
public enum SortDirection
{
    Ascending,
    Descending,
}
```

## `IOrderBy<T>`

```csharp
public interface IOrderBy<T>
{
    Expression<Func<T, object>> OrderByExpression { get; }
    SortDirection SortDirection { get; }
}
```

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `OrderByExpression` | `Expression<Func<T, object>>` | The expression selecting the property to order by. |
| `SortDirection` | `SortDirection` | Ascending or descending. |

## `OrderBy<T>`

```csharp
public class OrderBy<T> : IOrderBy<T>
{
    public OrderBy(Expression<Func<T, object>> orderByExpression, SortDirection sortDirection);
    public Expression<Func<T, object>> OrderByExpression { get; }
    public SortDirection SortDirection { get; }
}
```

Concrete `IOrderBy<T>` implementation. Both properties are read-only.

## `OrderBySpecification`

Static helper class with two factory methods for ergonomic ordering:

```csharp
public static class OrderBySpecification
{
    public static OrderBy<T> OrderBy<T>(Expression<Func<T, object>> expression, SortDirection sortDirection = SortDirection.Ascending);
    public static OrderBy<T> OrderByDescending<T>(Expression<Func<T, object>> expression, SortDirection sortDirection = SortDirection.Descending);
}
```

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `OrderBy(expression, sortDirection = Ascending)` | Creates an `OrderBy<T>` for ascending sort by default. |
| `OrderByDescending(expression, sortDirection = Descending)` | Creates an `OrderBy<T>` for descending sort by default. |

## Usage Example

```csharp
// Ascending
var data = await store.FindManyAsync(
    new AllSpecification<MyData>(),
    OrderBySpecification.OrderBy(x => x.CreatedAt));

// Descending
var dataDesc = await store.FindManyAsync(
    new AllSpecification<MyData>(),
    OrderBySpecification.OrderByDescending(x => x.CreatedAt));
```

